  "source_api_review": [
    "Concord 3.1.16 incrementally maintains exact ETF memory counts and an ordered conflict inventory for bounded ordinary statistics; 3.1.17 retains this repair.",
    "Recovery, snapshots, reconciliation and command admission retain exhaustive validation; derived statistics are not persisted in the unchanged v4 snapshot format.",
    "Concord 3.1.17 adds byte-ordered Turso indexes and optional node-local 32 MiB CAS admission. ESS retains file-backed VSR, 16 MiB replicated admission, its existing APIs and command versions 0/1.",
    "Gaoxy 0.15.2 admits the RC10 Abyss/Hell family through its published requirements, without HTTP overrides.",
    "HTTP RC10 adds a transitive http_pool package. ESS retains its existing bounded HTTP/1/HTTP/2 storage paths, raw response bytes, signing, redirect policy, ExSSL verification and stream timeouts.",
    "Bundler 10.1.5 and Phoenix DuskMoon 10.1.1 use the published native toolchain on Ubuntu 26.04/glibc 2.43.",
    "No dependency sources, resource bounds, quorum requirements, sampling coverage, original index workloads or runtime deadlines are changed."
  ],
